---
import ProjectLayout from "../../layouts/ProjectLayout.astro";
import ProjectTags from "../../components/ProjectTags.astro";
---

<ProjectLayout>
  <article class="space-y-12">
    <header>
      <h1 class="text-4xl sm:text-5xl font-bold mb-5">Hexapod: TOCATL</h1>
      <p class="text-lg leading-relaxed text-gray-700">TOCATL is an 18-actuator hexapod at UCLA’s Robotics and Mechanisms Laboratory, being prepared for an art museum installation in Korea. I built its Python and ROS 2 control and diagnostics stack and developed coordinated leg motions for the installation.</p>
      <ProjectTags />
    </header>

    <figure>
      <video autoplay loop controls muted playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/media/hexapod/spider-art-poster.jpg" class="w-full aspect-[4/3] object-contain">
        <source src="/media/hexapod/spider-art.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">Coordinated art motion on TOCATL.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Control and Diagnostics</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">The stack integrates two CAN buses with session calibration, motor feedback, and fault handling. Coordinated motion runs at a 100 Hz command rate, sending position and velocity targets with PD gains and torque feedforward to the motors’ internal controllers.</p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">I developed and tested bounded leg motions using motor feedback, alongside walking-gait baselines and expressive art motions. The motion plans define joint travel and timing so tests can progress from individual joints to coordinated movement.</p>
    </section>

    <figure>
      <img src="/media/hexapod/operator-preview.png" alt="TOCATL dashboard showing motion selection and controller state in preview mode" class="w-full h-auto" width="1280" height="720" loading="lazy" />
      <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">TOCATL operator dashboard.</figcaption>
    </figure>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Operator Interface</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">I built a browser interface to initialize CAN, capture the session reference, and preview motions before running them. It also provides selected-leg position capture, manual-motion recording, and downloadable logs.</p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Motion checks include calibrated joint limits and fresh motor feedback. Return and disable controls support supervised testing, with a physical power disconnect available because software stops depend on communication.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Logging and Testing</h2>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Run logs pair commanded motion with measured motor positions, reported torque, and temperature. Telemetry age, motor faults, CAN diagnostics, and loop timing help identify whether a problem comes from tracking, calibration, or communication.</p>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Those logs helped isolate command bursts after delayed control cycles. A pacing fix removed transmit-buffer errors in repeat tests, while intermittent missing replies remained under investigation.</p>
      <div class="grid gap-6 sm:grid-cols-2 pt-4">
        <figure>
          <a href="/media/hexapod/art-motion-loads.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open motor-load plot at full size">
            <img src="/media/hexapod/art-motion-loads.png" alt="Recorded motor q-axis current, reported torque, and estimated mechanical power over a Spider art motion test" class="w-full aspect-[4/3] object-contain bg-white" loading="lazy" />
          </a>
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">Art-motion test, August 24, 2026: combined load across 15 motors. Iq is motor q-axis current, not battery current.</figcaption>
        </figure>
        <figure>
          <a href="/media/hexapod/art-motion-thermal-voltage.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" aria-label="Open temperature and voltage plot at full size">
            <img src="/media/hexapod/art-motion-thermal-voltage.png" alt="Maximum reported temperature and minimum voltage for each of the 15 recorded motors" class="w-full aspect-[4/3] object-contain bg-white" loading="lazy" />
          </a>
          <figcaption class="mt-3 text-sm text-gray-500">Per-motor temperature and voltage from the same run.</figcaption>
        </figure>
      </div>
      <p class="leading-relaxed text-gray-700">Hardware tests demonstrated supported art motion. Walking-gait work remains in development.</p>
    </section>

    <section class="space-y-4">
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold">Walking simulation</h2>
      <video autoplay loop controls muted playsinline preload="metadata" poster="/media/hexapod/simulation.png" class="w-full aspect-video object-contain">
        <source src="/media/hexapod/walk-simulation.mp4" type="video/mp4" />
      </video>
      <p class="text-sm text-gray-500">Walking-gait development in MuJoCo.</p>
    </section>
  </article>
</ProjectLayout>
